  "title": "Pveg-EEBD-RBS0-SamyQ-Bopep4-Histag (9-23)-B0015",
  "description": "This **Protectant Module** constitutively expresses the stress-mitigation proteins and enables evaluation of their secretion and detection. The CDS encodes BoPep4, a 23-residue plant elicitor peptide (PEP) from broccoli (*Brassica oleracea var. italica).* The BoPep4 ([BBa\\_265CD14Z](https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-265cd14z)) protein is fused to the alpha-amylase signal peptide (SamyQ) at the N-terminus and a 6x Histag at the C-terminus. BoPep4 acts as a peptide hormone and signaling molecule to regulate plant defense mechanisms and salt tolerance. This version of BoPep4 was truncated from 15-23 amino acids.",
